  "text": "Seven-metric evaluation: AST-parse validity, AST-multiset Dice similarity, token similarity, weighted-Jaccard functional score, keyword F1, missing imports and input remnants, plus efficiency (pass rate per billion parameters) and a failure taxonomy separating token-budget truncation from real capability gaps. Stated limitation: similarity measures resemblance to a reference, not execution correctness — built for fair comparison between models; execution-based scoring was deferred. An 8-step deterministic post-processor raised validity ~70% → 95% and CodeBLEU 0.3058 → 0.3730 (+22%). System: Streamlit/React UI → FastAPI pipeline → PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector; hybrid RAG (pgvector cosine + tsvector full-text search); runtime hot-swapping across three fine-tuned models; Docker; Cloudflare Tunnel; six design iterations that removed a microservices setup (Redis, Celery, Nginx) in favour of four layers. Learnings: dataset diversity beats size (164 curated pairs); small fine-tuned models compete with large ones; deterministic post-processing is a force multiplier; hybrid retrieval beats vector-only; RAG can hurt simple inputs; base models in few-shot mode beat instruct models for this task; embedding choice matters."
